- How would you optimize memory to O(m*K) and still reconstruct the path?

## Why This Is Asked

Tests ability to model multi-block dynamic programming with non-trivial block scoring that depends on range statistics (max, min) and block length. It also covers reconstruction of the exact blocks, and invites discussion of time/space trade-offs.

## Key Concepts

- Partition DP with fixed k blocks
- Block score uses range (max-min) and length
- Inline maintenance of max/min while expanding the last block
- Path reconstruction with predecessor pointers

## Code Example

```javascript
function maxScore(A, k) {
  const n = A.length;
  const NEG = -1e15;
  const dp = Array.from({length: n+1}, () => Array(k+1).fill(NEG));
  const parent = Array.from({length: n+1}, () => Array(k+1).fill(-1));

  dp[0][0] = 0;

  for (let i = 1; i <= n; i++) {
    for (let t = 1; t <= k; t++) {
      let curMax = -INF, curMin = INF;
      for (let l = i; l >= 1; l--) {
        curMax = Math.max(curMax, A[l-1]);
        curMin = Math.min(curMin, A[l-1]);
        const blockScore = (curMax - curMin) * (i - l + 1);
        if (dp[l-1][t-1] + blockScore > dp[i][t]) {
          dp[i][t] = dp[l-1][t-1] + blockScore;
          parent[i][t] = l-1;
        }
      }
    }
  }

  // Reconstruct blocks
  const blocks = [];
  let i = n, t = k;
  while (t > 0) {
    const l = parent[i][t] + 1;
    blocks.unshift([l, i]);
    i = l - 1;
    t--;
  }

  return {maxScore: dp[n][k], blocks};
}
```

## Time/Space Complexity

Time: O(n²k) - for each i and t, we scan O(n) possible l values while maintaining max/min.

Space: O(nk) for dp table plus O(nk) for parent pointers if reconstruction needed, otherwise O(nk).

## Why This Is Asked
This tests fixed-length path DP and path reconstruction in graphs, a core DP pattern that shows depth beyond standard knapsack.

## Key Concepts
- DP on path length t
- State transition using edges
- Backpointer reconstruction
- Time and space trade-offs

## Code Example
```javascript
function maxKEdgePath(n, edges, k) {
  const NEG = -Infinity;
  const dp = Array.from({length: n}, () => Array(k+1).fill(NEG));
  const par = Array.from({length: n}, () => Array(k+1).fill(-1));
  for (let v=0; v<n; v++) dp[v][0] = 0;
  for (let t=1; t<=k; t++) {
    for (const e of edges) {
      const {u,v,w} = e;
      const prev = dp[u][t-1];
      if (prev !== NEG) {
        const cand = prev + w;
        if (cand > dp[v][t]) {
          dp[v][t] = cand;
          par[v][t] = u;
        }
      }
    }
  }
  let bestV = 0, best = NEG;
  for (let v=0; v<n; v++) if (dp[v][k] > best) { best = dp[v][k]; bestV = v; }
  const path = [];
  let cur = bestV;
  for (let t=k; t>=1; t--) { path.push(cur); cur = par[cur][t]; }
  path.push(cur);
  path.reverse();
  return {path, weight: best};
}
```

